    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e4ac14ac-c21a-5fe4-9101-1e886cd055ec",
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & 8 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & 8 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $5$th columns.",
